# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# A held callable takes every formal of its header. One that the named
# actuals leave out is refused as it is for a method, at the call.
fn: make2 (int: n) fn: (int: x; int: y) int
    fn: f2 (int: x; int: y) int
        return: n + x * 10 + y
    return: f2
@: h2 make2(100)
int: r h2(y: 2)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
